Sealed, no longer part of the product:

The natural-language expense parser and its corpus tooling were removed on
2026-08-21 when the product moved from free-text chat entry to a guided
flow. The code is not shipped and is not in this tree; it is kept, whole, in
`archive/chat-sealed-2026-08-21.tar.gz` and at the git tag
`pre-chat-removal-2026-08-21`. The attributions below are retained because
that archive still contains the ported code and the staged corpora.

- kor-to-number.js (https://github.com/dragonteros/kor-to-number.js)
  Copyright (c) dragonteros — MIT License
  The sino/native Korean number parsing core in
  src/lib/chat-parse/ko/numbers.ts is ported from kor-to-number.js's parsing
  logic, reworked to walk this codebase's Token[] array (bigint arithmetic,
  decoy-word rejection, and partial-token consumption are original additions
  not present upstream).

- open-korean-text (https://github.com/open-korean-text/open-korean-text)
