- words-to-numbers (https://github.com/0x80/words-to-numbers,
  npm package @codecompose/words-to-numbers)
  MIT License
  The English cardinal-number word grammar (ones/teens, tens+ones
  composition, hundred/thousand/million/billion/trillion tiering, "and"
  joiner, "point"/"dot" decimal marker) in src/lib/chat-parse/en/numbers.ts
  is ported from words-to-numbers' constants.js/parser.js/compiler.js
  region-matching logic, reworked to walk this codebase's Token[] array with
  exact bigint/scale arithmetic (the upstream compiler.js divides by
  Math.pow(10, n) for decimals, which this port does not — see money
  precision policy in docs/DECISIONS.md) and this codebase's own tier-state
  bigint arithmetic (ported from the same pattern already used by
  ko/numbers.ts's applyAtom/TierState). Bare "a" is deliberately NOT
  ported as a standalone value-1 word (upstream's UNIT.a = 1 would parse
  "a" in ordinary sentences like "a book" as the number 1) — "a" only
  contributes here as an explicit article immediately before a magnitude
  word ("a hundred", "a grand"), a narrower, original addition.

